{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789231794,"nonce":"O8Z9C7w0dd/czbN4bY/B/TDW4fQ=","title":"`let c: Any = 41` binds the raw integer, not a box","message":"def get_i(): i64 {\n        let c: Any = 41\n        return c\n    }\n\nlowers to `return const 41i32` with no box anywhere: the Let arm skips\ncoercion when the declared type is Any or Unknown, treating both as\n\"untyped\". Any is a declared type here, and a value bound to it must\nbox the way a call argument into an Any parameter does. Reading it\nback happens to work because the return unbox refuses a non-pointer\nvalue; passing `c` to a function taking Any hands it a raw integer as a\nbox pointer.","files":null}]}